/P 116 0 R
/T (Global research conducted with CEOs and C-suite executives points to a striking consensus: uncertainty is no longer a temporary disruption; it has become the permanent operating condition in which organizations function. Against this backdrop, this white paper brings together two complementary sources of insight.)
/E (Global research conducted with CEOs and C-suite executives points to a striking consensus: uncertainty is no longer a temporary disruption; it has become the permanent operating condition in which organizations function. Against this backdrop, this white paper brings together two complementary sources of insight.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 116 0 R
/T (The first consists of research published between 2025 and 2026 by leading global institutions, including McKinsey & Company, Gallup, PwC, Deloitte, The Conference Board, and the World Economic Forum. These studies provide a comprehensive view of the external realities confronting today's leaders, revealing how uncertainty, continuous change, and transformation pressures are reshaping organizations.)
/E (The first consists of research published between 2025 and 2026 by leading global institutions, including McKinsey & Company, Gallup, PwC, Deloitte, The Conference Board, and the World Economic Forum. These studies provide a comprehensive view of the external realities confronting today's leaders, revealing how uncertainty, continuous change, and transformation pressures are reshaping organizations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 116 0 R
/T (The second draws on the field of organizational neuroscience. This perspective explains how these external conditions influence the human brain, shaping the way leaders and employees perceive uncertainty, process information, regulate emotions, and make decisions.)
/E (The second draws on the field of organizational neuroscience. This perspective explains how these external conditions influence the human brain, shaping the way leaders and employees perceive uncertainty, process information, regulate emotions, and make decisions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 116 0 R
/T (By integrating these two perspectives, this report connects the strategic pressures emerging from the external business environment with their neurobiological consequences inside organizations. In doing so, it demonstrates why the brain-based design approach presented in the following chapters is not merely an academic framework, but a strategic imperative for organizations seeking to preserve decision quality, strengthen adaptability, and build sustainable competitive advantage in an age of continuous uncertainty.)
/E (By integrating these two perspectives, this report connects the strategic pressures emerging from the external business environment with their neurobiological consequences inside organizations. In doing so, it demonstrates why the brain-based design approach presented in the following chapters is not merely an academic framework, but a strategic imperative for organizations seeking to preserve decision quality, strengthen adaptability, and build sustainable competitive advantage in an age of continuous uncertainty.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
