/E (Manager engagement declined from 31% in 2022 to 22% in 2025, making it the primary driver of the global decline in employee engagement. According to Gallup, falling manager engagement is the single most significant factor behind the worldwide decrease in workforce engagement. In other words, managers are experiencing higher levels of burnout and disengagement, and these effects are cascading directly to their teams.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 535 0 R
/E (Gallup also found that managers who receive training in artificial intelligence are approximately 50% less likely to become actively disengaged. AI-enabled and well-supported managers report greater confidence, adapt more effectively to change, and are significantly less likely to disconnect from their work.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
