273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 118 0 R
/T (As stress intensifies, the brain shifts away from deliberate analysis toward rapid, instinctive responses. As a result, leaders may become more risk-averse, postpone difficult decisions, avoid conflict, or default to familiar solutions rather than exploring new alternatives. In many cases, these behaviors do not reflect a lack of leadership capability; they are the predictable biological response of a brain operating under sustained cognitive overload.)
