1738 0 obj
<<
/Title (The foundations of change management were built in a business environment where change was less frequent, more predictable, and where initiatives had clearly defined starting and ending points. Today, however, organizations operate in an environment of continuous disruption driven by technological transformation, artificial intelligence, geopolitical uncertainty, new business models, and ongoing restructuring.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1596 0 R
/Next 1903 0 R
>>
endobj
1739 0 obj
<<
/Title (Uncertainty will not disappear. However, organizations can design how people think, make decisions, and collaborate within uncertain environments. The organizations of the future will not be those that simply manage change; they will be those that design systems capable of enabling healthy decision-making even in the face of continuous uncertainty.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1596 0 R
/Prev 1904 0 R
>>
endobj
