/Title (In this new reality, the critical question is no longer how effectively organizations manage change, but how effectively they can make sound decisions under uncertainty. Neuroscience shows us that the brain does not primarily respond to change itself, but to uncertainty. As uncertainty increases, attention narrows, cognitive load rises, threat perception intensifies, and decision quality declines.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1596 0 R
/Prev 1903 0 R
/Next 2029 0 R
>>
endobj
2029 0 obj
<<
/Title (Therefore, sustainable performance does not come from communicating more, but from designing systems that enable the brain to continue functioning effectively under these conditions.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1596 0 R
/Prev 2028 0 R
/Next 1904 0 R
>>
