/Title (In situations we classify as risk, the possible outcomes are known. The probability of success may be low, but the likelihood of different outcomes can still be estimated and evaluated. Uncertainty, by contrast, is characterized by the absence of reliable information about what will happen, when it will happen, or what the consequences will be.)
