2162 0 obj
<<
/Title (A study published in the Journal of Neuroscience in January 2025 found that leaders within the same organization do not necessarily make the same decisions, even when presented with identical information. The explanation extends beyond differences in experience or personality. The interaction between the brain's threat detection system and its cognitive control networks influences whether an individual is more likely to take risks or avoid them under conditions of uncertainty. Consequently, some leaders are able to move forward despite incomplete information, while others tend to delay decisions in pursuit of additional certainty.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2129 0 R
/Prev 2161 0 R
/Next 2147 0 R
>>
endobj
2163 0 obj
<<
/Title (Lower-quality decisions)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2112 0 R
/Prev 2148 0 R
/Next 2171 0 R
>>
endobj
2164 0 obj
